---
import LegalPage from '../../components/LegalPage.astro';
import { site } from '../../config/site';
const contact = site.contact.email;
---

<LegalPage title="Privacy policy" updated="October 2026">
  <p>
    This policy explains what {site.fullName} ("HG", "we") collects when you visit this website, why, and what you can
    ask us to do with it. We collect as little as we can.
  </p>

  <h2>What we collect</h2>
  <p>
    <strong>Browsing.</strong> The site sets no cookies and runs no analytics, advertising or tracking scripts. Our hosting
    provider keeps standard technical server logs (such as IP address, time and page requested) for security and
    reliability.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Your bag.</strong> The contents of your bag are stored only in your own browser (local storage) so they are
    still there when you return. They are not sent to us until you choose to check out.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Newsletter and "notify me".</strong> If you subscribe, we receive your email address and the date you signed
    up. We use it only to write to you about HG. Every email includes a way to unsubscribe.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Orders.</strong> Payment is handled by Stripe on its secure checkout page. Stripe receives your payment,
    billing and shipping details; we receive the order details needed to fulfil and support your order. We never see or
    store your full card number.
  </p>

  <h2>Why we use it</h2>
  <p>
    To provide the site and keep it secure, to take and deliver orders, and, only if you asked for it, to send you our
    letters. We do not sell your personal data.
  </p>

  <h2>Who we share it with</h2>
  <p>
    Service providers that act on our behalf: our hosting provider, Stripe for payments, and our email provider for the
    newsletter. Each may process data outside your country under appropriate safeguards.
  </p>

  <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
  <p>
    Newsletter addresses until you unsubscribe. Order records for as long as the law requires for accounting and tax.
    Server logs for a short period.
  </p>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>
    Depending on where you live, you may ask to access, correct, delete or export your data, or object to its use. You can
    also complain to your local data protection authority.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    {
      contact ? (
        <>
          Write to us at <a class="link" href={`mailto:${contact}`}>{contact}</a>.
        </>
      ) : (
        <>Contact details will be published here before launch.</>
      )
    }
  </p>
</LegalPage>
